<title>IRAQ: PRESS DIGEST - Iraq -Dec 4.</title>
<headline>PRESS DIGEST - Iraq -Dec 4.</headline>
<dateline>BAGHDAD 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>These are some of the leading stories in the official Iraqi press on Wednesday. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy.</p>
<p>THAWRA</p>
<p>- Iraqi dinar continues soaring against foreign currencies.</p>
<p>- Prices of foodstuffs decline further.</p>
<p>- Plan to produce 1.5 million tonnes of barley and wheat this season.</p>
<p>- Iraq and Vietnam discuss imports of rice to Iraq.</p>
<p>- Health minister opens pharmaceutical exhibition.</p>
<p>- Japaneses businessmen to visit Iraq for oil deals.</p>
<p>- Decline in crime in Iraq following Baghdad's acceptance of oil-for-food deal.</p>
<p>JUMHOURIYA</p>
<p>- Saudi Arabia welcomes Iraq's oil deal with U.N.</p>
</text>
